You can get rid of most things simply by putting it in a box.  I have yet
not seen any monster open a box.  A sack or bag should also work.  Keep some bags,
and put unwanted stuff into one of them.  When it gets too heavy, just drop it
and use the next bag.  The shops usually pay a lot for wands and scrolls,
so I wouldn't destroy them if I were you.  Monsters don't usually get items
from shops, but you can leave a bag or box in the shop to be safe.

You may use up a wand by zapping it repeatedly.  A potion
break when you kick it, or you may dilute it in a fountain and leave it.
Potions of water isn't dangerous.  Scrolls are destroyed by writing on them
when they aren't blank.  A weapon may be effectively destroyed by
repeatedly engraving with it.  It will get so many minuses that it will be
almost harmless.  Weapons and armor may also be vaporized by over-enchanting.

You may also throw items into a pool of water.  The items will be inaccessible to
most monsters.  Potions will dilute, books and scrolls will be blank, and
weapons and armor will rust into uselessness.
